# Line endings, and the one class of file that must not have them rewritten.
#
# There was no `.gitattributes` here at all, so `core.autocrlf` decided — and on
# Windows it decides CRLF. That is harmless for source, which every compiler in
# this tree reads either way, and it is corruption for a wire capture.
#
# A `.sse` file is bytes an endpoint actually sent. Server-sent events are framed
# by a blank line, so the frame boundary IS the line ending; a replay test that
# asserts what a consumer delivered from those bytes is asserting on the exact
# bytes. `anthropic_fixture_replay` and `google_fixture_replay` do precisely
# that, and four of their negative controls — the ones that prove a broken
# consumer produces specific wrong output — fail on a Windows checkout and pass
# on Linux. They were written off as environmental for most of this project's
# life. They are not: git was editing the evidence.
#
# The same argument covers `.jsonl`, which is a record per line, and the
# recorded transcripts under `docs/regression-baseline/`, which
# `scripts/check-transcripts.sh` compares byte for byte to prove the mock
# harness is still deterministic. A checkout that rewrote them would make that
# script report a behaviour change nobody made.
#
# `-text` rather than `text eol=lf` on purpose: these are captures, not source.
# `eol=lf` would still let git *decide* they are text and normalise on commit;
# `-text` says do not touch these bytes, in either direction, ever. The cost is
# that git renders their diffs as binary, which is the correct reading of a file
# whose value is its exact contents.
#
# Deliberately only these two patterns, and no `* text=auto`. Measured before
# writing this: every one of the 36 stored objects is already pure LF, so the
# corruption is entirely in the checkout and nothing needs re-committing. Adding
# a repo-wide rule staged 37 unrelated transcript files for renormalisation —
# including the ones `scripts/check-transcripts.sh` compares byte for byte to
# prove the mock harness is deterministic. Fixing a line-ending bug by rewriting
# the evidence that would detect one is not a fix.
*.sse -text
*.jsonl -text
